Get ready, because today we're diving deep into HR phrases.

434
00:20:57,460 --> 00:20:58,780
Oh, sounds interesting.

435
00:20:58,800 --> 00:21:01,070
We've got two guides packed with example.

436
00:21:01,200 --> 00:21:01,830
Oh.

437
00:21:01,850 --> 00:21:02,950
And we're going to decode them.

438
00:21:03,550 --> 00:21:03,730
Awesome.

439
00:21:03,750 --> 00:21:06,510
Not just their meanings, but like the strategy behind them.

440
00:21:06,730 --> 00:21:07,250
I like it.

441
00:21:07,270 --> 00:21:10,200
It's like your secret decoder ring for the workplace.

442
00:21:10,780 --> 00:21:11,080
Yeah.

443
00:21:11,100 --> 00:21:15,010
From job hunting to performance reviews and everything in between.

444
00:21:15,090 --> 00:21:16,310
That's a lot of ground to cover.

445
00:21:16,290 --> 00:21:18,030
It is, but it's going to be fun.

446
00:21:18,330 --> 00:21:18,950
Okay, I'm ready.

447
00:21:19,210 --> 00:21:20,580
So let's start at the very beginning.

448
00:21:20,820 --> 00:21:21,220
Okay.

449
00:21:21,320 --> 00:21:21,880
Recruitment.

450
00:21:21,920 --> 00:21:23,590
We've all seen those job postings.

451
00:21:23,610 --> 00:21:23,970
Yeah.

452
00:21:24,350 --> 00:21:28,560
You know the ones we are looking for a qualified candidate for the position of?

453
00:21:28,710 --> 00:21:30,770
Ugh, so boring.

454
00:21:30,810 --> 00:21:31,590
I know, right?

455
00:21:32,010 --> 00:21:33,090
It's like a robot wrote it.

456
00:21:33,270 --> 00:21:34,270
Exactly.

457
00:21:34,310 --> 00:21:37,520
So in today's world, don't you think companies need to stand out a bit more?

458
00:21:37,680 --> 00:21:38,020
Definitely.

459
00:21:38,040 --> 00:21:42,020
They need to grab your attention, make you actually want to apply.

460
00:21:42,080 --> 00:21:46,700
So how can they use language to make a job posting more captivating?

461
00:21:46,830 --> 00:21:50,930
Well, instead of just stating the obvious, they need to paint a picture.

462
00:21:50,970 --> 00:21:53,110
Ooh, I like that.

463
00:21:53,190 --> 00:21:57,040
You know, highlight the challenges, the opportunities, the impact the person will make.

464
00:21:57,380 --> 00:21:58,100
That makes sense.

465
00:21:58,120 --> 00:22:00,250
It's about sparking that feeling.

466
00:22:00,350 --> 00:22:00,930
What feeling?

467
00:22:01,130 --> 00:22:03,260
That I want to be part of that feeling.

468
00:22:03,450 --> 00:22:04,180
Ooh, I get it.

469
00:22:04,220 --> 00:22:05,300
Like a sense of purpose.

470
00:22:05,400 --> 00:22:06,040
Exactly.

471
00:22:06,380 --> 00:22:07,830
Okay, now what about that other classic?

472
00:22:08,130 --> 00:22:08,550
Which one?

473
00:22:09,090 --> 00:22:11,570
The Ideal Candidate Should Possess.

474
00:22:11,990 --> 00:22:13,280
Oh, yeah, that one.

475
00:22:13,300 --> 00:22:15,120
It seems like every job description has it.

476
00:22:15,360 --> 00:22:16,000
Pretty much.

477
00:22:16,420 --> 00:22:19,970
But I've noticed some are just laundry lists of requirements.

478
00:22:19,990 --> 00:22:20,310
Yeah.

479
00:22:20,810 --> 00:22:22,320
While others are more strategic.

480
00:22:22,580 --> 00:22:23,160
Interesting.

481
00:22:23,240 --> 00:22:24,060
What's the difference?

482
00:22:24,430 --> 00:22:31,000
Well, instead of focusing solely on qualifications, companies should focus on the desired outcomes.

483
00:22:31,580 --> 00:22:32,180
Like what?

484
00:22:32,300 --> 00:22:33,950
What will this person achieve?

485
00:22:34,690 --> 00:22:36,390
What problems will they solve?

486
00:22:36,990 --> 00:22:37,410
Interesting.

487
00:22:37,430 --> 00:22:42,400
By framing it that way, they attract candidates who are excited about the impact they can make.

488
00:22:42,880 --> 00:22:46,050
It's like they're not just filling a role, they're joining a mission.

489
00:22:46,210 --> 00:22:47,010
Exactly.

490
00:22:47,120 --> 00:22:47,730
I like that.

491
00:22:47,910 --> 00:22:49,710
Aligning expectations from the start.

492
00:22:49,870 --> 00:22:50,530
Absolutely.

493
00:22:50,590 --> 00:22:51,930
And then, of course, there's the deadline.

494
00:22:51,990 --> 00:22:52,190
Yeah.

495
00:22:52,330 --> 00:22:55,080
Applications will be accepted until... Can't forget that.

496
00:22:55,240 --> 00:22:57,300
But is there more to it than just a date?

497
00:22:57,580 --> 00:22:58,600
More than you might think.

498
00:22:58,900 --> 00:22:59,200
Really?

499
00:22:59,400 --> 00:23:01,880
It's about subtly communicating expectations.

500
00:23:02,530 --> 00:23:02,910
Like what?

501
00:23:03,590 --> 00:23:06,310
Well, respecting deadlines shows you're organized.

502
00:23:06,510 --> 00:23:06,930
Makes sense.

503
00:23:07,410 --> 00:23:12,880
On the flip side, a company that's vague about deadlines might signal a lack of organization.

504
00:23:13,080 --> 00:23:14,120
Ooh, that's a good point.

505
00:23:14,160 --> 00:23:14,900
It's like a red flag.

506
00:23:14,980 --> 00:23:15,560
Exactly.

507
00:23:15,940 --> 00:23:17,490
Okay, so let's say you've applied.

508
00:23:17,810 --> 00:23:17,990
No.

509
00:23:18,070 --> 00:23:19,030
And you get that email.

510
00:23:19,310 --> 00:23:19,670
Oh, yeah.

511
00:23:19,990 --> 00:23:21,770
We would like to invite you for an interview.

512
00:23:22,250 --> 00:23:23,760
The moment you've been waiting for.

513
00:23:23,820 --> 00:23:27,260
It is, but even this phrase can be approached strategically.

514
00:23:27,700 --> 00:23:28,310
How so?

515
00:23:28,680 --> 00:23:31,210
What can companies do to make it stand out?

516
00:23:31,830 --> 00:23:33,390
Instead of a generic invitation.

517
00:23:33,450 --> 00:23:33,890
Okay.

518
00:23:34,110 --> 00:23:35,500
Why not add a personal touch?

519
00:23:35,860 --> 00:23:36,220
Like what?

520
00:23:36,320 --> 00:23:40,140
Mention something specific about the candidate's application, their background.

521
00:23:40,240 --> 00:23:40,480
I see.

522
00:23:40,520 --> 00:23:41,800
It shows they've actually read it.

523
00:23:41,920 --> 00:23:43,590
Yeah, that would make me feel valued.

524
00:23:43,610 --> 00:23:44,030
Exactly.

525
00:23:44,250 --> 00:23:46,410
Okay, then comes the scheduling back and forth.

526
00:23:46,730 --> 00:23:49,160
Oh yeah, the dreaded scheduling dance.

527
00:23:49,540 --> 00:23:51,260
Please confirm your availability.

528
00:23:51,300 --> 00:23:52,240
So many emails.

529
00:23:52,320 --> 00:23:53,320
Any hidden insights here?

530
00:23:53,720 --> 00:23:55,180
Think of it as a test.

531
00:23:55,570 --> 00:23:56,330
Of what?

532
00:23:56,350 --> 00:23:57,590
Your communication skills.

533
00:23:57,930 --> 00:23:58,410
Interesting.

534
00:23:58,630 --> 00:24:02,320
Being prompt and professional shows respect for everyone's time.

535
00:24:02,560 --> 00:24:02,780
Right.

536
00:24:02,820 --> 00:24:03,960
It's like the first impression.

537
00:24:04,160 --> 00:24:04,680
Exactly.

538
00:24:04,910 --> 00:24:05,210
Okay.

539
00:24:05,270 --> 00:24:06,870
And then the big moment, the interview.

540
00:24:07,370 --> 00:24:07,870
Here we go.

541
00:24:08,310 --> 00:24:12,180
You're likely to hear, could you elaborate on your experience with...

542
00:24:13,170 --> 00:24:13,990
That's a classic.

543
00:24:14,070 --> 00:24:15,270
Any advice for how to handle it?

544
00:24:15,470 --> 00:24:16,660
Be prepared.

545
00:24:17,020 --> 00:24:17,400
For what?

546
00:24:17,540 --> 00:24:23,160
To share specific examples of how you've used your skills to achieve results.

547
00:24:23,440 --> 00:24:24,970
So it's not just about listing skills.

548
00:24:25,070 --> 00:24:26,690
No, it's about telling a story.

549
00:24:27,170 --> 00:24:27,630
I like that.

550
00:24:27,650 --> 00:24:29,650
A story that showcases your abilities.

551
00:24:29,790 --> 00:24:30,850
And makes you memorable.

552
00:24:31,040 --> 00:24:31,650
Exactly.

553
00:24:31,900 --> 00:24:33,320
Okay, so let's fast forward.

554
00:24:33,640 --> 00:24:33,920
Two.

555
00:24:33,940 --> 00:24:34,700
You land the job.

556
00:24:35,040 --> 00:24:35,440
Woo-hoo.

557
00:24:35,840 --> 00:24:37,640
And you hear, welcome aboard.

558
00:24:38,740 --> 00:24:39,790
Feels good.

559
00:24:40,190 --> 00:24:43,330
But is this just a formality or is there more to it?

560
00:24:43,570 --> 00:24:44,590
It's the gateway.

561
00:24:44,630 --> 00:24:45,330
To what?

562
00:24:45,350 --> 00:24:47,720
A successful onboarding experience.

563
00:24:48,260 --> 00:24:48,600
Ah, I see.

564
00:24:48,620 --> 00:24:51,660
It's about making the new employee feel valued.

565
00:24:51,800 --> 00:24:52,380
Part of the team.

566
00:24:52,720 --> 00:24:53,340
Exactly.

567
00:24:53,400 --> 00:24:55,070
So what comes after welcome aboard?

568
00:24:55,350 --> 00:25:02,050
Well, things like, let's go over your onboarding schedule or please review the employee handbook.

569
00:25:02,410 --> 00:25:03,500
Yeah, those are important.

570
00:25:03,520 --> 00:25:04,320
They're opportunities.

571
00:25:04,760 --> 00:25:05,320
To do what?

572
00:25:05,420 --> 00:25:10,140
set clear expectations, answer questions, make the transition smooth.

573
00:25:10,640 --> 00:25:13,540
So it's about structure and support right from the start.

574
00:25:13,560 --> 00:25:14,080
Absolutely.

575
00:25:14,220 --> 00:25:17,330
But how can companies go beyond the standard handbook?

576
00:25:17,630 --> 00:25:19,470
You mean make it more engaging?

577
00:25:19,490 --> 00:25:20,410
Yeah, more impactful.

578
00:25:20,430 --> 00:25:25,210
Well, instead of a dense document, imagine an interactive online handbook.

579
00:25:25,930 --> 00:25:26,340
With what?

580
00:25:26,660 --> 00:25:30,760
Videos, quizzes, maybe even a forum for new hires to connect.

581
00:25:31,020 --> 00:25:31,540
I love that.

582
00:25:31,800 --> 00:25:33,700
Turning something boring into something fun.

583
00:25:33,850 --> 00:25:35,690
It's about welcoming them into the culture.

584
00:25:35,970 --> 00:25:36,710
That's a great point.

585
00:25:36,730 --> 00:25:37,980
It's not just about compliance.

586
00:25:38,020 --> 00:25:38,900
It's about belonging.

587
00:25:39,500 --> 00:25:39,800
Okay.

588
00:25:39,840 --> 00:25:41,180
So onboarding is crucial.

589
00:25:41,500 --> 00:25:42,100
Definitely.

590
00:25:42,320 --> 00:25:45,410
But it's also about setting employees up for success.

591
00:25:45,530 --> 00:25:45,970
Yes.

592
00:25:46,190 --> 00:25:48,410
Which brings us to performance management.

593
00:25:48,730 --> 00:25:48,850
Right.

594
00:25:48,870 --> 00:25:49,970
What's the strategy behind it?

595
00:25:49,990 --> 00:25:52,340
Let's discuss your performance goals for this quarter.

596
00:25:53,020 --> 00:25:54,660
It signals a shift.

597
00:25:54,680 --> 00:25:55,100
From what?

598
00:25:55,200 --> 00:25:58,630
A top-down approach to a collaborative one.

599
00:25:58,830 --> 00:25:59,270
Interesting.

600
00:25:59,550 --> 00:26:06,200
It's about aligning expectations and making sure the employee understands how their work contributes to the bigger picture.

601
00:26:06,260 --> 00:26:07,750
So it's a two-way conversation.

602
00:26:07,970 --> 00:26:08,430
Exactly.

603
00:26:08,450 --> 00:26:09,290
Not a dictate.

604
00:26:09,310 --> 00:26:09,490
Right.

605
00:26:09,590 --> 00:26:10,670
Everyone loves recognition.

606
00:26:11,130 --> 00:26:11,540
Of course.

607
00:26:11,560 --> 00:26:16,550
But hearing your contributions have been highly valued can sometimes feel generic.

608
00:26:16,810 --> 00:26:17,130
Yeah.

609
00:26:17,310 --> 00:26:18,730
It needs to be more specific.

610
00:26:19,010 --> 00:26:21,150
How can companies make it more meaningful?

611
00:26:21,220 --> 00:26:24,340
Highlight a specific action or achievement.

612
00:26:24,820 --> 00:26:25,160
Like what?

613
00:26:25,480 --> 00:26:30,390
Maybe the way you handled that client issue was exceptional and it really saved the day.

614
00:26:30,750 --> 00:26:31,150
Oh, wow.

615
00:26:31,250 --> 00:26:31,930
That's much better.

616
00:26:32,350 --> 00:26:34,010
It's more impactful and memorable.

617
00:26:34,470 --> 00:26:36,500
Okay, so now for the elephant in the room.

618
00:26:37,060 --> 00:26:37,580
Oh, boy.

619
00:26:37,680 --> 00:26:39,020
There's room for improvement.

620
00:26:39,200 --> 00:26:41,300
Nobody likes hearing that.

621
00:26:41,320 --> 00:26:43,950
It's true, but it's a reality of work life.

622
00:26:44,750 --> 00:26:45,490
Unfortunately.

623
00:26:45,790 --> 00:26:49,270
So how can managers deliver this feedback constructively?

624
00:26:49,490 --> 00:26:51,310
Frame it as an opportunity for growth.

625
00:26:51,730 --> 00:26:52,030
Okay.

626
00:26:52,170 --> 00:26:57,260
Instead of focusing on what went wrong, focus on how to improve.

627
00:26:57,280 --> 00:26:58,580
Do you think you can give me an example?

628
00:26:58,760 --> 00:26:59,000
Sure.

629
00:26:59,040 --> 00:27:02,880
Like, I've noticed that your presentations sometimes lose focus.

630
00:27:03,340 --> 00:27:06,850
Let's work together to develop some techniques to keep your audience engaged.

631
00:27:07,230 --> 00:27:07,850
That's much better.

632
00:27:07,950 --> 00:27:09,050
It's about offering support.

633
00:27:09,190 --> 00:27:09,710
Exactly.

634
00:27:09,870 --> 00:27:10,090
All right.

635
00:27:10,150 --> 00:27:12,270
Now let's dive into employee relations.

636
00:27:12,830 --> 00:27:12,930
Okay.

637
00:27:12,950 --> 00:27:14,610
What's the message behind employee relations?

638
00:27:15,230 --> 00:27:17,200
we encourage open communication.

639
00:27:17,420 --> 00:27:18,780
It's a statement of values.

640
00:27:19,380 --> 00:27:19,720
Meaning?

641
00:27:19,760 --> 00:27:23,220
The company values feedback and welcomes ideas.

642
00:27:23,840 --> 00:27:25,490
But it's not enough to just say it, right?

643
00:27:25,770 --> 00:27:26,790
No, they have to show it.

644
00:27:27,270 --> 00:27:32,130
By actively listening, responding to feedback, creating safe spaces for dialogue.

645
00:27:32,430 --> 00:27:35,240
So walking the walk, not just talking the talk.

646
00:27:35,400 --> 00:27:35,920
Exactly.

647
00:27:35,960 --> 00:27:37,200
Conflicts are bound to happen.

648
00:27:37,220 --> 00:27:38,200
In any workplace, yes.

649
00:27:38,560 --> 00:27:42,420
What's the significance of, let's address this matter professionally?

650
00:27:43,160 --> 00:27:44,060
It sets the tone.

651
00:27:44,270 --> 00:27:44,660
For what?

652
00:27:44,850 --> 00:27:47,890
A respectful and solution-oriented approach.

653
00:27:47,910 --> 00:27:48,510
I see.

654
00:27:48,530 --> 00:27:51,800
It's about acknowledging the issue and encouraging dialogue.

655
00:27:51,980 --> 00:27:53,180
While staying professional.

656
00:27:53,420 --> 00:27:53,940
Of course.

657
00:27:54,100 --> 00:27:57,460
What about, this is a safe space to discuss your concerns.

658
00:27:57,660 --> 00:27:59,410
It's about creating a culture of trust.

659
00:27:59,950 --> 00:28:01,990
So employees feel safe to speak up.

660
00:28:02,530 --> 00:28:02,850
Exactly.

661
00:28:02,870 --> 00:28:04,090
Without fear of repercussions.

662
00:28:04,230 --> 00:28:04,890
Right.

663
00:28:04,910 --> 00:28:06,480
Okay, so we've covered a lot of ground.

664
00:28:06,960 --> 00:28:07,560
We have.

665
00:28:07,700 --> 00:28:10,020
From recruitment to employee relations.

666
00:28:10,180 --> 00:28:11,260
And everything in between.

667
00:28:11,900 --> 00:28:15,810
It's fascinating how much strategy and nuance is packed into these phrases.

668
00:28:15,930 --> 00:28:16,590
It really is.

669
00:28:16,630 --> 00:28:17,900
Ready to keep exploring.

670
00:28:18,020 --> 00:28:18,500
Absolutely.

671
00:28:18,520 --> 00:28:18,940
Let's do it.

672
00:28:18,960 --> 00:28:20,180
Let's go behind the scenes a bit.

673
00:28:20,200 --> 00:28:20,300
Okay.

674
00:28:20,320 --> 00:28:21,020
What do you have in mind?

675
00:28:21,370 --> 00:28:24,990
Phrases you might not hear every day but are still super important.

676
00:28:25,010 --> 00:28:25,360
Got it.

677
00:28:25,540 --> 00:28:27,280
Like, have you ever heard of an ATS?

678
00:28:27,400 --> 00:28:27,480
Yes.

679
00:28:28,220 --> 00:28:29,960
Uh, maybe.

680
00:28:30,300 --> 00:28:30,940
Vaguely.

681
00:28:31,120 --> 00:28:32,910
Applicant tracking system.

682
00:28:32,930 --> 00:28:33,390
Oh, right.

683
00:28:33,430 --> 00:28:34,770
But what is it exactly?

684
00:28:34,890 --> 00:28:37,760
Think of it like a digital gatekeeper for resumes.

685
00:28:38,120 --> 00:28:38,420
Hmm.

686
00:28:38,640 --> 00:28:39,080
Is that all?

687
00:28:39,200 --> 00:28:45,870
It uses algorithms to scan through tons of applications, hundreds, even thousands sometimes.

688
00:28:45,970 --> 00:28:46,410
Wow.

689
00:28:46,510 --> 00:28:48,470
So it's not just about having a good resume.

690
00:28:48,450 --> 00:28:51,080
It's about having a resume the ATS understands.

691
00:28:51,380 --> 00:28:52,060
So how do you do that?

692
00:28:52,340 --> 00:28:55,310
Pay close attention to the keywords in the job description.

693
00:28:55,460 --> 00:28:57,010
Make sure those are in your resume.

694
00:28:57,230 --> 00:28:58,890
Use clear language.

695
00:28:59,070 --> 00:29:01,120
Avoid jargon or weird formatting.

696
00:29:01,640 --> 00:29:04,020
So basically make it easy for the ATS to find your skills.

697
00:29:04,300 --> 00:29:04,900
Exactly.

698
00:29:05,340 --> 00:29:05,640
All right.

699
00:29:05,720 --> 00:29:06,930
Let's talk about onboarding.

700
00:29:07,430 --> 00:29:09,270
We talked about the basics.

701
00:29:09,450 --> 00:29:10,930
Welcome aboard the handbook.

702
00:29:11,270 --> 00:29:12,760
But there's more to it than that, right?

703
00:29:12,940 --> 00:29:14,620
Onboarding is a process.

704
00:29:14,880 --> 00:29:15,700
Not just an event.

705
00:29:15,920 --> 00:29:16,400
Exactly.

706
00:29:16,460 --> 00:29:17,670
It's an ongoing journey.

707
00:29:17,730 --> 00:29:18,490
Of what?

708
00:29:18,810 --> 00:29:20,870
Integrating new hires into the company.

709
00:29:20,950 --> 00:29:22,780
The culture, the work, everything.

710
00:29:22,880 --> 00:29:23,100
Yep.

711
00:29:23,120 --> 00:29:24,200
Setting them up for success.

712
00:29:25,140 --> 00:29:25,440
I see.

713
00:29:25,580 --> 00:29:27,710
But sometimes companies just focus on the logistics.

714
00:29:27,990 --> 00:29:29,710
Paperwork, forms, all that.

715
00:29:29,930 --> 00:29:30,170
Yeah.

716
00:29:30,350 --> 00:29:31,770
How can they make it more engaging?

717
00:29:31,990 --> 00:29:32,830
Get creative.

718
00:29:33,670 --> 00:29:35,630
Use gamification challenges.

719
00:29:36,360 --> 00:29:39,800
Maybe new hires earn points for completing modules.

720
00:29:39,940 --> 00:29:40,300
Okay.

721
00:29:40,540 --> 00:29:43,140
Or do a scavenger hunt to learn about different departments.

722
00:29:43,220 --> 00:29:43,690
Oh, that's fun.

723
00:29:43,970 --> 00:29:45,810
It makes it more interactive and memorable.

724
00:29:45,830 --> 00:29:46,510
I like it.

725
00:29:46,970 --> 00:29:47,170
All right.

726
00:29:47,190 --> 00:29:49,270
Let's talk about keeping employees engaged.

727
00:29:49,750 --> 00:29:50,300
Retention.

728
00:29:50,540 --> 00:29:50,780
Right.

729
00:29:51,060 --> 00:29:51,660
Exactly.

730
00:29:51,720 --> 00:29:52,960
What's the key phrase here?

731
00:29:53,240 --> 00:29:54,700
Employee value proposition.

732
00:29:54,740 --> 00:29:55,960
EVP.

733
00:29:56,220 --> 00:29:56,660
That's it.

734
00:29:57,160 --> 00:29:57,940
But what does it mean?

735
00:29:58,390 --> 00:30:00,530
It's why someone would want to work at your company.

736
00:30:00,760 --> 00:30:02,070
Beyond just the salary.

737
00:30:02,090 --> 00:30:02,290
Right.

738
00:30:02,390 --> 00:30:05,820
The culture, the great opportunities, the meaningful work.

739
00:30:05,840 --> 00:30:07,070
So it's the whole package.

740
00:30:07,270 --> 00:30:10,000
It's what attracts and keeps good people.

741
00:30:10,090 --> 00:30:11,700
A lot of companies struggle with this, don't they?

742
00:30:11,800 --> 00:30:13,040
Defining their EVP.

743
00:30:13,180 --> 00:30:13,480
Yeah.

744
00:30:13,620 --> 00:30:14,120
They do.

745
00:30:14,200 --> 00:30:15,240
What's the best way to do it?

746
00:30:15,700 --> 00:30:16,860
Listen to your employees.

747
00:30:17,460 --> 00:30:17,800
Okay.

748
00:30:17,880 --> 00:30:18,900
What do they value?

749
00:30:19,680 --> 00:30:20,120
Makes sense.

750
00:30:20,530 --> 00:30:23,050
Use that to create an EVP that resonates.

751
00:30:23,530 --> 00:30:24,570
Authentic and aligned.

752
00:30:24,830 --> 00:30:25,450
Exactly.

753
00:30:25,830 --> 00:30:25,970
Okay.

754
00:30:25,990 --> 00:30:28,070
How about this stay interview?

755
00:30:28,820 --> 00:30:29,640
Interesting one.

756
00:30:29,700 --> 00:30:30,820
Seems counterintuitive.

757
00:30:30,980 --> 00:30:31,600
It is a bit.

758
00:30:31,740 --> 00:30:32,180
I do them.

759
00:30:32,380 --> 00:30:34,080
Instead of waiting for someone to quit.

760
00:30:34,380 --> 00:30:34,580
Right.

761
00:30:34,600 --> 00:30:36,840
You talk to them about what's working, what's not.

762
00:30:36,820 --> 00:30:38,310
Before they even think about leaving.

763
00:30:38,510 --> 00:30:39,110
Exactly.

764
00:30:39,170 --> 00:30:40,030
It's proactive.

765
00:30:40,110 --> 00:30:41,150
But would people be honest?

766
00:30:41,270 --> 00:30:42,260
That's where trust comes in.

767
00:30:42,280 --> 00:30:43,660
A safe space to talk.

768
00:30:43,700 --> 00:30:43,860
Right.

769
00:30:43,920 --> 00:30:46,140
It's a conversation, not an interrogation.

770
00:30:46,180 --> 00:30:46,480
Okay.

771
00:30:46,500 --> 00:30:47,990
Let's talk about growth and development.

772
00:30:49,290 --> 00:30:50,810
Creep having is a big one.

773
00:30:50,830 --> 00:30:51,410
It is.

774
00:30:51,760 --> 00:30:52,980
But what does it actually mean?

775
00:30:53,090 --> 00:30:56,660
Empowering employees to own their careers.

776
00:30:57,260 --> 00:30:59,120
Help them figure out their goals.

777
00:30:59,360 --> 00:31:01,540
Provide guidance, resources.

778
00:31:01,660 --> 00:31:02,310
Exactly.

779
00:31:02,350 --> 00:31:04,570
And create opportunities for them to grow.

780
00:31:04,610 --> 00:31:07,130
So it's more than just an annual review.

781
00:31:07,370 --> 00:31:07,850
Much more.

782
00:31:07,890 --> 00:31:10,040
How can companies make it ongoing?

783
00:31:10,020 --> 00:31:14,040
Mentorship programs, skill assessments, job shadowing.

784
00:31:14,220 --> 00:31:14,520
I see.

785
00:31:14,700 --> 00:31:16,790
Even internal talent marketplaces.

786
00:31:16,940 --> 00:31:17,290
What's that?

787
00:31:17,490 --> 00:31:22,150
Where employees can express interest in different projects or roles.

788
00:31:22,970 --> 00:31:23,590
Oh, I like that.

789
00:31:23,690 --> 00:31:25,400
It's about continuous learning.

790
00:31:25,500 --> 00:31:26,880
Essential in today's world.

791
00:31:26,920 --> 00:31:27,420
Absolutely.

792
00:31:27,440 --> 00:31:29,860
We can't forget about recognition.

793
00:31:30,520 --> 00:31:31,180
Important one.

794
00:31:31,260 --> 00:31:32,480
Recognition program.

795
00:31:33,070 --> 00:31:34,830
But how do you make it meaningful?

796
00:31:35,190 --> 00:31:36,080
Make it personal.

797
00:31:36,920 --> 00:31:38,420
Peer to peer recognition.

798
00:31:38,480 --> 00:31:42,030
Spot bonuses, timely rewards.

799
00:31:42,390 --> 00:31:44,870
So not just a generic employee of the month.

800
00:31:45,010 --> 00:31:46,850
No, it needs to be specific and genuine.

801
00:31:47,430 --> 00:31:47,630
All right.

802
00:31:47,650 --> 00:31:49,200
Let's talk about the other side of retention.

803
00:31:49,240 --> 00:31:49,860
The flip side.

804
00:31:50,020 --> 00:31:51,060
Employee turnover.

805
00:31:51,300 --> 00:31:51,600
Yeah.

806
00:31:51,700 --> 00:31:53,200
What's the significance of this phrase?

807
00:31:53,290 --> 00:31:55,370
It tells you how healthy your organization is.

808
00:31:55,550 --> 00:31:55,830
Really?

809
00:31:56,110 --> 00:31:58,350
High turnover means something's wrong.

810
00:31:58,570 --> 00:31:58,970
Like what?

811
00:31:59,410 --> 00:32:02,920
Low morale, no growth opportunities, bad management.

812
00:32:02,940 --> 00:32:03,800
There's a warning sign.

813
00:32:04,080 --> 00:32:04,320
It is.

814
00:32:04,400 --> 00:32:06,200
You need to figure out why people are leaving.

815
00:32:06,340 --> 00:32:06,860
And fix it?

816
00:32:07,400 --> 00:32:07,970
Exactly.

817
00:32:08,250 --> 00:32:09,930
Create a place where people want to stay.

818
00:32:10,130 --> 00:32:10,370
Okay.

819
00:32:10,510 --> 00:32:12,330
All of this happens within the context of?

820
00:32:12,850 --> 00:32:13,210
Of what?

821
00:32:13,330 --> 00:32:14,880
Organizational culture.

822
00:32:14,890 --> 00:32:15,900
Ah, the big one.

823
00:32:16,240 --> 00:32:18,280
It's a buzzword, but what does it really mean?

824
00:32:18,430 --> 00:32:21,470
It's the invisible force that shapes everything.

825
00:32:21,790 --> 00:32:22,230
Everything.

826
00:32:22,290 --> 00:32:23,210
How decisions are made.

827
00:32:23,430 --> 00:32:23,690
Okay.

828
00:32:23,710 --> 00:32:24,630
How people interact.

829
00:32:25,060 --> 00:32:26,440
It's the personality of the company.

830
00:32:26,460 --> 00:32:26,960
You got it.

831
00:32:27,540 --> 00:32:29,200
So how do you create a positive culture?

832
00:32:29,400 --> 00:32:30,520
It starts with leadership.

833
00:32:31,280 --> 00:32:35,010
Leaders who live the values, communicate clearly, create a sense of purpose.

834
00:32:35,150 --> 00:32:36,890
It's not just about perks and fun stuff.

835
00:32:37,030 --> 00:32:38,630
No, it's much deeper than that.

836
00:32:38,870 --> 00:32:41,410
All right, let's move on to performance evaluations.

837
00:32:41,430 --> 00:32:41,890
Okay.

838
00:32:42,040 --> 00:32:44,100
Key performance indicators.

839
00:32:44,330 --> 00:32:45,150
KPIs.

840
00:32:45,230 --> 00:32:46,450
What's the strategy with those?

841
00:32:46,580 --> 00:32:49,960
KPIs are a way to track progress.

842
00:32:50,380 --> 00:32:51,160
Towards goals.

843
00:32:51,280 --> 00:32:53,610
Right, but they need to be the right KPIs.

844
00:32:53,670 --> 00:32:53,990
Meaning?

845
00:32:54,210 --> 00:32:57,270
Aligned with individual role and business objectives.

846
00:32:57,450 --> 00:32:59,150
So not just random metrics.

847
00:32:59,170 --> 00:33:01,620
No, they should be meaningful and drive performance.

848
00:33:01,840 --> 00:33:04,220
What about 360 degree feedback?

849
00:33:04,620 --> 00:33:05,270
That's a good one.

850
00:33:05,530 --> 00:33:06,630
Seems more holistic.

851
00:33:06,760 --> 00:33:08,900
It is, you get feedback from everyone.

852
00:33:08,920 --> 00:33:10,060
Your boss, your peers.

853
00:33:10,420 --> 00:33:11,540
Even your subordinates.

854
00:33:11,720 --> 00:33:13,500
Wow, that's a lot of feedback.

855
00:33:13,520 --> 00:33:14,960
It gives you a well-rounded view.

856
00:33:15,330 --> 00:33:16,610
But could it get messy?

857
00:33:16,630 --> 00:33:18,330
It can if it's not done right.

858
00:33:18,510 --> 00:33:19,430
So how do you do it right?

859
00:33:19,970 --> 00:33:22,370
Clear guidelines, constructive criticism.

860
00:33:22,830 --> 00:33:24,790
Focus on development, not judgment.

861
00:33:25,390 --> 00:33:25,950
Exactly.

862
00:33:26,020 --> 00:33:29,080
For new hires, there's often a probation period.

863
00:33:29,280 --> 00:33:30,640
Yeah, that's standard.

864
00:33:30,720 --> 00:33:31,460
What's the purpose?

865
00:33:31,480 --> 00:33:32,560
It's a trial period.

866
00:33:32,680 --> 00:33:33,540
For both sides.

867
00:33:33,640 --> 00:33:35,800
Right, the employee and the employer.

868
00:33:35,850 --> 00:33:37,370
So they can see if it's a good fit.

869
00:33:37,710 --> 00:33:38,520
Exactly.

870
00:33:38,600 --> 00:33:40,480
But wouldn't that make new hires anxious?

871
00:33:40,700 --> 00:33:44,070
It could, but clear communication is key.

872
00:33:44,270 --> 00:33:45,390
So they know what's expected.

873
00:33:45,650 --> 00:33:47,310
Regular check-ins are important too.

874
00:33:47,330 --> 00:33:48,970
Make it a collaborative experience.

875
00:33:49,090 --> 00:33:49,790
Exactly.

876
00:33:49,810 --> 00:33:51,780
Okay, what happens when performance isn't good?

877
00:33:52,680 --> 00:33:53,960
Then you might have a PIP.

878
00:33:54,890 --> 00:33:56,250
Performance improvement plan.

879
00:33:56,370 --> 00:33:56,550
Yep.

880
00:33:57,250 --> 00:33:58,490
But it shouldn't be scary.

881
00:33:58,780 --> 00:33:59,300
How so?

882
00:33:59,600 --> 00:34:01,600
It's an opportunity to get back on track.

883
00:34:01,700 --> 00:34:03,290
With support and clear goals.

884
00:34:03,570 --> 00:34:03,770
Right.

885
00:34:03,810 --> 00:34:05,820
It's about improvement, not punishment.

886
00:34:06,240 --> 00:34:06,760
I like that.

887
00:34:06,820 --> 00:34:08,640
Now what about when someone's doing great?

888
00:34:09,250 --> 00:34:10,330
Time for a reward.

889
00:34:10,510 --> 00:34:11,930
Like merit-based pay.

890
00:34:12,210 --> 00:34:12,970
That's one way.

891
00:34:13,370 --> 00:34:14,820
But it can be controversial.

892
00:34:14,970 --> 00:34:15,360
It can.

893
00:34:15,430 --> 00:34:16,200
It needs to be fair.

894
00:34:16,420 --> 00:34:16,700
Meaning?

895
00:34:16,840 --> 00:34:20,100
Based on clear criteria, transparently communicated.

896
00:34:20,280 --> 00:34:21,480
So everyone knows how it works.

897
00:34:21,500 --> 00:34:22,020
Exactly.

898
00:34:22,280 --> 00:34:22,510
All right.

899
00:34:22,530 --> 00:34:24,510
Let's talk about compliance and policy.

900
00:34:24,990 --> 00:34:25,250
Okay.

901
00:34:25,270 --> 00:34:26,770
Starting with EEO.

902
00:34:27,130 --> 00:34:28,710
Equal Employment Opportunity.

903
00:34:28,910 --> 00:34:30,540
What does that actually mean in practice?

904
00:34:30,940 --> 00:34:32,480
It means everyone has a fair chance.

905
00:34:33,160 --> 00:34:34,520
Regardless of their background.

906
00:34:34,540 --> 00:34:34,660
Right.

907
00:34:34,720 --> 00:34:35,540
No discrimination.

908
00:34:35,980 --> 00:34:38,110
So how do you create a culture of EEO?

909
00:34:38,270 --> 00:34:43,190
Leadership commitment, diversity training, open dialogue, accountability.

910
00:34:44,300 --> 00:34:46,810
It's about creating a truly inclusive workplace.

911
00:34:46,990 --> 00:34:47,910
That's the goal.

912
00:34:48,040 --> 00:34:51,210
Speaking of inclusivity, workplace harassment policy.

913
00:34:51,510 --> 00:34:52,510
Can't forget that one.

914
00:34:52,650 --> 00:34:55,070
But just having a policy isn't enough.

915
00:34:55,300 --> 00:34:56,740
No, you need to enforce it.

916
00:34:56,840 --> 00:34:58,240
And create a culture of respect.

917
00:34:58,340 --> 00:34:58,740
Exactly.

918
00:34:58,780 --> 00:35:01,490
Provide training, clear reporting mechanisms.

919
00:35:01,830 --> 00:35:03,450
So people feel safe to speak up.

920
00:35:04,010 --> 00:35:04,550
Absolutely.

921
00:35:04,650 --> 00:35:06,190
Code of conduct is another important one.

922
00:35:06,210 --> 00:35:07,520
Sets the ethical standards.

923
00:35:07,720 --> 00:35:10,100
But how do you make it more than just words on paper?

924
00:35:10,080 --> 00:35:10,960
Live it every day.

925
00:35:11,600 --> 00:35:12,120
Meanwhile.

926
00:35:12,140 --> 00:35:13,040
Review it regularly.

927
00:35:13,120 --> 00:35:14,750
Provide training.

928
00:35:15,130 --> 00:35:15,970
Hold people accountable.

929
00:35:15,990 --> 00:35:17,570
Make ethics part of your DNA.

930
00:35:17,630 --> 00:35:19,310
What about the grievance procedure?

931
00:35:19,830 --> 00:35:21,930
Important for resolving issues fairly.

932
00:35:22,070 --> 00:35:24,720
So employees have a way to voice concerns.

933
00:35:25,280 --> 00:35:26,800
Without fear of retaliation.

934
00:35:26,840 --> 00:35:28,620
And finally, compliance training.

935
00:35:29,740 --> 00:35:30,700
Everyone's favorite.

936
00:35:31,480 --> 00:35:32,680
I know, but it's necessary.

937
00:35:33,050 --> 00:35:35,450
It is, but how do you make it less boring?

938
00:35:35,920 --> 00:35:36,780
That's the challenge.

939
00:35:36,920 --> 00:35:37,740
Get creative.

940
00:35:37,780 --> 00:35:38,100
Again.

941
00:35:38,140 --> 00:35:38,940
Always.

942
00:35:39,700 --> 00:35:41,950
Use scenarios, games, make it relevant.

943
00:35:42,050 --> 00:35:43,810
So people actually learn something.

944
00:35:43,830 --> 00:35:44,390
Exactly.

945
00:35:44,450 --> 00:35:46,220
Turn it into a positive experience.

946
00:35:46,400 --> 00:35:46,720
Wow.

947
00:35:46,760 --> 00:35:47,980
We've covered so much.

948
00:35:48,100 --> 00:35:48,700
We have.

949
00:35:48,820 --> 00:35:50,240
From A to Z of HR.

950
00:35:50,460 --> 00:35:52,270
It's amazing how much these phrases matter.

951
00:35:52,530 --> 00:35:53,130
They really do.

952
00:35:53,170 --> 00:35:55,390
They shape the whole employee experience.

953
00:35:55,540 --> 00:35:58,070
I used to think they were just about being formal, you know.

954
00:35:58,090 --> 00:35:58,870
It's this procedure.

955
00:35:59,090 --> 00:35:59,330
Yeah.

956
00:35:59,490 --> 00:36:00,630
But now I see them differently.

957
00:36:00,810 --> 00:36:01,450
How so?

958
00:36:01,490 --> 00:36:03,710
They're tools for creating a good workplace.

959
00:36:03,850 --> 00:36:05,800
A positive and productive environment.

960
00:36:06,120 --> 00:36:06,560
Exactly.

961
00:36:06,620 --> 00:36:08,980
And anyone can benefit from understanding them.

962
00:36:09,140 --> 00:36:09,600
That's true.

963
00:36:09,900 --> 00:36:10,720
No matter your role.

964
00:36:10,800 --> 00:36:13,470
It's about communication and understanding the dynamics.

965
00:36:13,490 --> 00:36:14,910
I feel like we've only scratched the surface.

966
00:36:15,510 --> 00:36:16,110
We have.

967
00:36:16,130 --> 00:36:17,490
There's always more to explore.

968
00:36:17,550 --> 00:36:19,450
This has been a great deep dive, though.

969
00:36:19,580 --> 00:36:19,920
I agree.

970
00:36:20,000 --> 00:36:20,500
It's been fun.

971
00:36:20,660 --> 00:36:24,180
So as we wrap up, any final thoughts for our listeners?

972
00:36:24,400 --> 00:36:26,540
Just pay attention to the language around you.

973
00:36:26,960 --> 00:36:27,580
At work.

974
00:36:27,600 --> 00:36:29,990
Everywhere, really, but especially at work.

975
00:36:30,010 --> 00:36:31,210
What should we be listening for?

976
00:36:31,690 --> 00:36:32,930
Not just the words themselves.

977
00:36:33,010 --> 00:36:34,270
But the meaning behind them.

978
00:36:34,290 --> 00:36:36,330
Exactly, the intentions, the impact.

979
00:36:36,510 --> 00:36:37,880
It's like being a language detective.

980
00:36:38,240 --> 00:36:38,820
Kind of.

981
00:36:39,160 --> 00:36:40,880
Being mindful of the power of words.

982
00:36:41,060 --> 00:36:41,500
I like that.

983
00:36:41,740 --> 00:36:43,300
Using language to make work better.

984
00:36:43,440 --> 00:36:44,100
For everyone.

985
00:36:45,110 --> 00:36:45,530
Well said.

986
00:36:45,570 --> 00:36:47,690
Thanks for joining us on this deep dive, everyone.

987
00:36:47,710 --> 00:36:48,410
It's been a pleasure.

988
00:36:48,950 --> 00:36:52,680
Remember, clear communication is key to a thriving workplace.

989
00:36:53,260 --> 00:36:54,240
Until next time.

990
00:36:58,470 --> 00:36:59,500
Thank you.
